Reject SBR frames without valid frequency tables.

An ADTS header marks SBR active on every frame (get_adts_header.cpp),
also after an SBR header that sbr_reset_dec() rejected or a fallback to
upsampling. The next frames then ran the high-band generation and the
envelope adjustment with half-updated or stale tables, and indexed past
the QMF and envelope buffers:
- init_sbr_dec.cpp marks the tables unset (noSubbands = 0), and
  sbr_read_data.cpp keeps them unset after a failed reset; a frame
  without a successful reset is rejected as an invalid bitstream.
- sbr_applied.cpp falls back to upsampling when SBR is active without
  tables (frames that carry no SBR element).
- sbr_update_freq_scale.cpp: with too few bands, the band adjustment
  walked off diff_tot; it now reports an empty master table.
- sbr_reset_dec.cpp rejects a decreasing master table (negative bands,
  ISO/IEC 14496-3, 4.6.18.3.2) and more than MAX_NOISE_COEFFS noise
  bands.

Regression input: tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-stale-tables.bin.

